==French==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|fr|frm|saulver}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|sauver}}, {{m|fro|salver}}, from Gallo-Romance {{m|fro|salvar}}, from {{inh|fr|LL.|salvō|salvāre|to save}}, from {{inh|fr|la|salvus}}.

In the sense specific to North America, a {{semantic loan|nocap=1|fr|en|save}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|fr|Fr-sauver.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{fr-verb}}

# to [[save]], [[rescue]]; to [[protect]]
# {{lb|fr|computing}} to save
#: {{syn|fr|sauvegarder}}
# {{lb|fr|pronominal}} to [[escape]], [[run away]]
# {{lb|fr|North America}} to save {{gloss|conserve, prevent the wasting of}}
#: {{syn|fr|économiser|préserver}}
